WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:05.420
Car tester Reinhold Deisenhofer says even
James Bond doesn't get a new company car every

00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:10.830
day -- and the Aston Martin DB11's predecessor,
the DB9, showed it.

00:00:10.830 --> 00:00:16.090
Its platform was developed for the Vanquish
back in 2001, and its motorization was even

00:00:16.090 --> 00:00:20.140
older -- from the era when Aston Martin belonged
to Ford.

00:00:20.140 --> 00:00:24.550
In the meantime, Daimler has bought into the
British carmaker, and that's fine if you consider

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:26.850
the current AMG GT models.

00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:29.860
Let's see what the DB11 can do, he says.

00:00:34.020 --> 00:00:40.660
The official successor to the DB9 is impressive
at first sight -- and not just when it's sunny.

00:00:40.660 --> 00:00:46.620
The DB11 is classically elegant, with proverbial
Britsh understatement.

00:00:46.620 --> 00:00:51.360
Its design language will be the basis for
all future Aston Martin models.

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:53.990
No sills or spoilers.

00:00:53.990 --> 00:00:59.290
Out of consideration for the neighbors, the
car is even programmed for a silent start:

00:00:59.290 --> 00:01:03.610
for the first few meters, the noise flaps
in the exhaust remain closed.

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:05.900
But later -- watch out!

00:01:14.820 --> 00:01:18.170
Then the engine roars from all 12 cylinders.

00:01:18.170 --> 00:01:24.569
This gentleman-racecar churns out 447 kilowatts
and takes just 3-point-9 seconds to rocket

00:01:24.569 --> 00:01:26.689
to 100 kilometers an hour.

00:01:26.689 --> 00:01:32.609
Its 700 Newton-meters of torque and top speed
of 322 kilometers an hour promise fantastic

00:01:32.609 --> 00:01:35.140
-- if eccentric -- driving fun.

00:01:36.829 --> 00:01:41.220
Reinhold says the Aston Martin Gran Turismo's
interior is classical.

00:01:41.220 --> 00:01:47.040
The perfect bucket seats and leather ceiling
make you go "Ahhh!" when you sit down.

00:01:47.040 --> 00:01:50.240
And the instruments are very reduced.

00:01:50.249 --> 00:01:54.030
The central console has five buttons made
of real glass.

00:01:54.030 --> 00:01:56.920
The middle one -- the ignition -- is surrounded
by those controlling

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:59.620
the 8-speed automatic transmission.

00:02:00.980 --> 00:02:04.400
Reinhold is especially taken with the precise
steering.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:09.420
The only thing he can find to criticize is
that there are too few surfaces to store things..

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:15.300
The cooperation between Mercedes and Aston
Martin has paid off.

00:02:15.319 --> 00:02:19.599
The interior feels more modern than in the
DB11's predecessors.

00:02:19.599 --> 00:02:22.750
New are the 12-inch infotainment and digital
instruments.

00:02:22.750 --> 00:02:26.110
But the model hasn't lost any of its British
charm.

00:02:26.110 --> 00:02:28.800
There's top-quality leather wherever you look.

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:35.240
The British end of the partnership gets all
the credit for the DB11's handling.

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:39.280
The car is much faster and more agile than
you'd imagine at first sight.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:42.450
Overall, it seems very different from its
competitors.

00:02:42.450 --> 00:02:46.959
There's none of that Ferrari melodrama or
gut-wrenching Lamborghini roar.

00:02:46.959 --> 00:02:51.300
In the DB11, even very high speeds seem routine.

00:03:08.500 --> 00:03:14.080
Reinhold says the DB11 definitely has the
"James Bond" feel of an Aston Martin.

00:03:14.080 --> 00:03:19.680
It's a lovely GT with the performance of a
super sportscar and the elegance of a timeless icon.

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:24.980
But even when driving at moderate speeds,
fuel consumption never dropped below 14 liters

00:03:24.989 --> 00:03:26.750
per 100 kilometers.

00:03:26.750 --> 00:03:32.709
He tells us the "DB" stands for David Brown,
who bought the Aston Martin company in 1947.

00:03:32.709 --> 00:03:38.640
In 1963, the DB5 became the first James Bond
car -- and served in the films Goldfinger

00:03:38.640 --> 00:03:39.480
and Thunderball.

